{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 36c833bb: not accepted. Pending cells, a bounded raw read and a changed late-answer rule are too much machinery in authority.ts for a liveness residual. This ruling narrows b4a6626d, which asked for more than the problem is worth.\n\nDo this instead, in R3b:\n1. Keep the run-wide `generation` for Membership reads that are in flight. A read whose generation moved while it waited still returns null. That rule is what stops an older active answer for an evicted key, and one counter does it.\n2. Change only the handles. `held()` and `sealed()` no longer compare the generation. A handle of an admitted key depends on that key's kept record and never on the denied FIFO. A handle of a denied key is valid while the FIFO still holds the record that the handle was made from.\n3. Add no pending cell, no reader count and no new deadline. Do not import `within` or `LATE` into authority.ts. A late Membership answer behaves as it does on main.\n\nAssertions: one changes. Admitted key 5000's handle stays current after an eviction. The fresh key0 read that causes an eviction still returns null for itself, as R3a asserts today. The older key0 read still returns null.\n\nControl: the R3a eviction control stays as it is, because `generation++` stays. Run no other control for this change. R3b's own control is the unbounded-insertion control from 1f159465.\n\nResidual, one sentence in the threat-model paragraph: an eviction from the denied FIFO makes the Membership reads in flight at that instant unanswered for every key, and each caller retries. Handles already held stay valid. Only an act from a distinct revoked key that the FIFO does not hold causes an eviction.\n\nIf your source reading shows that item 2 needs more than about ten changed lines, or that a handle cannot reach its record, stop and report. The fallback is the checker's option 1: no code change and the sentence alone.\n\nSlot: the R3a deployment ended at 16:43:43 (END 1fff0ff8). Book T0a's focused plan now.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}